  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — namely, the skewness of the lotteries — is not considered by the individual. The individual does not mention the distribution of probabilities around the favorable outcome or evaluate whether one lottery has a greater concentration of probability on the positive outcome (i.e., left-skew). Instead, the individual focuses only on the absolute difference in winning probabilities (1%) and the small difference in prize amounts. The decision reason requires assessing skewness (i.e., whether the favorable outcome has a higher probability relative to the zero outcome), which is not present in the verbal report. The individual’s justification is based on a simple comparison of probabilities and prize amounts, not on a rule about skewness. Therefore, the decision reason was not used. The individual did not apply the rule that prefers the more left-skewed lottery, even though B is slightly more left-skewed. There is no reference to skewness in the reasoning process.",
